  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Sunday)\nIssued at 1015 AM MDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nDeep moisture will shift east today via a northern stream \nshortwave and associated sfc trough. This will transition the \nregion into WNW flow aloft and allow for occasional cool fronts \nlater in the week. Another monsoon wave will push NE into the \nregion this afternoon and interact with a sfc trough dropping into\nthe region. This will force showers and storms across the FA with\nthe best chances across NW SD late this afternoon and scentral SD\novernight. A few stronger storms are possible this afternoon \nacross NW SD where increased flow aloft may allow storms to \norganize for a bit, supporting gusty winds and small hail. Things \nwill dry out NW-SE into Tue, with lingering shower chances reaming\nacross far eastern scentral SD through Tue morning. Seasonal and \ndry Tue and Wed. Cool fronts will knock down temps Thur, and again\nthis weekend, with highs in the 60s behind these systems. Some \nlight rain may develop with the NW flow impulses if enough forcing\nand moisture is realized, but these systems will be mainly dry.",
